network_troubleshooting_notes


the console port and mgmt port both lead to OOB management interfaces

mgmt port - network OOB
  - you connect via ssh
  - when you connect, you land in the BMC shell
  - mgmt port --> BMC (has it's own isolated cpu, ram, and OS)

console port 
  - serial / direct OOB
  - does not speak TCP/IP
  - to connect, you have to use a serial terminal client to run the Serial Protocol (not ssh) and a specific baud rate
  - when you connect, you land in the host OS
  - console port --> UART chip --> BMC --> motherboard --> CPU
  - this connection to the CPU is on as long as there is electrons flowing through the CPU. You can watch as the BIOS boots or as the host OS crashes
  - very slow bandwidth. Meant for text based interface only

data plane ports
  - you connect via ssh or rdp
  - when you connect, you land in the host OS
  - ETH port --> NIC --> motherboard --> --> RAM --> CPU
  - this connection is only possible if multiple network and device conditions are setup properly. If any of the conditions are misconfigured, you immediately lose connection and access. See below
  - can have very high bandwidth. Meant for the bulk of the data to flow. Can use GUIs through this path


What Needs to Be Working Inside the OS?
Requirement⬇️	                           Host OS via Console (Serial)⬇️	                                     Host OS via Production Ethernet (In-Band)⬇️
OS State	                                Single-user mode, recovery mode, or early boot	                       Fully booted multi-user OS
NIC Drivers	                              ❌ Not needed	                                                         Must be loaded & initialized
IP / Subnet Config	                      ❌ Not needed	                                                         Valid IP/Gateway must be assigned
Host Firewall (iptables/ufw)	            ❌ Completely bypasses it	                                           Port 22/3389 must be allowed
Routing / Switching	                      ❌ Not needed	                                                         Upstream switches, VLANs, and routers must be functional
SSH Daemon (sshd)	                        ❌ Not needed (managed by getty/agetty)	                               Must be running and healthy

Production Ethernet: If someone typo’s a firewall rule (ufw enable locking out port 22), accidentally deletes the default gateway, misconfigures a bond/VLAN, or if sshd crashes, your connection drops and you are locked out.
Console: Because it is handled by the kernel via a basic serial terminal service (like ttyS0), none of the network stack matters. If the network completely breaks, the console still works.




